{#
  The plain-text alternative. Not decoration: a text/plain part is what keeps a
  mail out of the spam filters that penalise HTML-only messages, and it is what
  a text-mode or screen-reader client actually reads. Same blocks as the HTML
  layout, minus the presentation.

  Spacing is written with deliberate blank lines because Twig swallows the first
  newline after a `%}` tag — the version that looked right in the source arrived
  as "…with Olena Kovalenko.Persepolis" in the inbox.
#}
